# Date Entry = Date Picker

Anywhere the user enters a date (or date range), use a date picker widget — never a free-text input.

- Prefer the native `<input type="date">` styled to the site's brand; it's clean, simple, accessible, and needs no dependencies.
- Ranges get two pickers (start → end); swap silently if end < start.
- If a display label is needed (e.g. "Aug 4–7"), compose it from the picked dates in code — don't ask the user to type it.

```html
<!-- ❌ BAD -->
<input placeholder="date label" value="Aug 4–7">

<!-- ✅ GOOD -->
<input type="date" aria-label="start date"> →
<input type="date" aria-label="end date">
```
